Install and update (Windows)
----------------------------
Keep this folder together: the setup program copies game_files\ from the
folder it runs in. Run Ssx3-@VERSION@-setup.exe. It installs for your user
only (no administrator rights) to %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Ssx3 and adds a
Start Menu entry. Running a newer setup installs on top and keeps your
saves. Uninstall from Settings > Apps; your saves and settings stay in
%LOCALAPPDATA%\Ssx3.

Windows may warn before running the setup program or Ssx3.exe: they are
built on your machine and not signed. SmartScreen: "More info" > "Run
anyway". If the folder came as a .zip downloaded or copied from another
machine, right-click the .zip > Properties > Unblock before extracting
(Mark of the Web), or Windows asks again for every file.

To keep saves and settings somewhere else, set SSX3_DATA_DIR (a Windows
environment variable) to that folder before starting the game.

Settings
--------
This build has no options file. Launcher settings are KEY=value lines in
config\launch.env in %LOCALAPPDATA%\Ssx3; launch.env.default in the install
folder lists the defaults.

Note: this is an early port. It has been tested on a Mac (Metal) with a
scripted controller from the title screen into a race. This Direct3D 11
build has not been run yet, under Proton (DXVK) or on native Windows, and
a full play-through has not been tried. On a Steam Deck use the steamos
bundle: its README has the Deck notes.

Controls
--------
Use a controller (XInput pad 1). The game reads only the pad.

Speed
-----
The game steps a fixed amount per frame. On a machine that cannot keep up,
races play in slow motion but correctly.
